# Shell scripts must keep LF line endings, including on a Windows checkout (G-81).
*.sh text eol=lf
*.awk text eol=lf   # read by awk in the Linux containers of packaging/linux (G-331)

# C# source keeps LF on every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says (G-145). A raw-string literal ("""...""")
# takes the line endings of its file, and tests edit those strings with text that contains \n; on a CRLF
# checkout such an edit matches nothing, the test passes or fails without testing the change.
*.cs text eol=lf
